<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hari Singh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1895">1895</a>–<a href="/years/1961">1961</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Maharaja Hari Singh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hari Singh was the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jammu">Jammu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a>, reigning from 1925 to 1952. At the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/partition-of-india">partition of India</a> in 1947 he hesitated between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, hoping for independence. After Pashtun tribal forces invaded from Pakistan in October 1947, he signed the Instrument of Accession to India, which led to the first India–Pakistan war over Kashmir.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hari-singh.jpg" alt="Hari Singh" width="320" height="464" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georges Devred · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hari_Singh_1931.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
